    <DataNode elementId="AT5G13700-MONOMER" textLabel="Polyamine oxidase 1" type="Protein">
      <Xref identifier="Q9FNA2" dataSource="uniprot" />
      <Graphics centerX="150" centerY="215" width="90.0" height="25.0" textColor="000000" fontName="Arial" fontWeight="Normal" fontStyle="Normal" fontDecoration="Normal" fontStrikethru="Normal" fontSize="12" hAlign="Center" vAlign="Middle" borderColor="000000" borderStyle="Solid" borderWidth="1.0" fillColor="FFFFFF" shapeType="Rectangle" />
      <Comment source="pmngroup">|FRAME: AT5G13700-MONOMER spermine oxidase| (PAO) is a flavin adenine dinucleotide-dependent enzyme involved in polyamine catabolism. A database search within the Arabidopsis genome sequence showed the presence of a gene (|FRAME: AT5G13700 PAO1|) encoding a putative PAO with 45% amino acid sequence identity with the maize gene |FRAME: G-7161 MPAO|. The |FRAME: AT5G13700 PAO1| cDNA was isolated and expressed in Escherichia coli. The recombinant protein was purified and was shown to be a flavoprotein able to oxidize |FRAME: SPERMINE spermine|, |FRAME: CPD-10689 norspermine|, and |FRAME: N1-ACETYLSPERMINE &lt;i&gt;N&lt;/i&gt;&lt;sup&gt;1&lt;/sup&gt;-acetylspermine| |CITS: [16778015]| The enzyme has a substrate oxidation mode similar to that of animal |FRAME: G-11043 SMOX|-encoded PAOs (which produce |FRAME: CPD-6082 3-aminopropanal|) and different from currently characterized plant polyamine oxidases, which produce |FRAME: CPD-313 propane-1,3-diamine| (see |FRAME: MONOMER-9461 polyamine oxidase (propane-1,3-diamine forming)|).</Comment>
      <Property key="UniqueID" value="AT5G13700-MONOMER" />
